{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01P8gpZ7b3aaJ266cKw9htQn","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t/*\n2\t * Source: https://github.com/risc0/risc0 (ref=093f46925a0366d72df505256d35c54a033ddad0)\n3\t * Status: MODIFIED from risc0/sys/kernels/zkp/cuda/fpext.h\n4\t * Imported: 2025-01-25 by @gaxiom\n5\t * \n6\t * LOCAL CHANGES (high level):\n7\t * - 2025-03-25: add operator-()\n8\t * - 2025-09-19: use sppark's bb31_4_t impl for core arithmetic operations\n9\t */\n10\t\n11\t// Copyright 2024 RISC Zero, Inc.\n12\t//\n13\t// Licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0 (the \"License\");\n14\t// you may not use this file except in compliance with the License.\n15\t// You may obtain a copy of the License at\n16\t//\n17\t//     http://www.apache.org/licenses/LICENSE-2.0\n18\t//\n19\t// Unless required by applicable law or agreed to in writing, software\n20\t// distributed under the License is distributed on an \"AS IS\" BASIS,\n21\t// WITHOUT WARRANTIES OR CONDITIONS OF ANY KIND, either express or implied.\n22\t// See the License for the specific language governing permissions and\n23\t// limitations under the License.\n24\t\n25\t#pragma once\n26\t\n27\t/// \\file\n28\t/// Defines FpExt, a finite field F_p^4, based on Fp via the irreducible polynomial x^4 - 11.\n29\t\n30\t#include \"fp.h\"\n31\t\n32\t/// Instances of FpExt are element of a finite field F_p^4.  They are represented as elements of\n33\t/// F_p[X] / (X^4 - 11). Basically, this is a 'big' finite field (about 2^128 elements), which is\n34\t/// used when the security of various operations depends on the size of the field.  It has the field\n35\t/// Fp as a subfield, which means operations by the two are compatible, which is important.  The\n36\t/// irreducible polynomial was chosen to be the simplest possible one, x^4 - B, where 11 is the\n37\t/// smallest B which makes the polynomial irreducible.\n38\tstruct FpExt {\n39\t    /// The elements of FpExt, elems[0] + elems[1]*X + elems[2]*X^2 + elems[3]*x^4\n40\t    union {\n41\t        Fp elems[4];\n42\t        bb31_4_t rep;\n43\t    };\n44\t    \n45\t    /// Default constructor makes the zero elements\n46\t    __device__ FpExt() : rep(bb31_t{0u}) {}\n47\t\n48\t    /// Initialize from uint32_t\n49\t    __device__ explicit FpExt(uint32_t x) : rep(bb31_t{x}) {}\n50\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01CxAp3cyzXvfpYeFo9ZYegw","session_id":"d346b169-4c5b-4579-98c0-3e4f65b0717e","uuid":"abf75e12-9fd0-4c13-9ea6-34cdff92d04f","timestamp":"2026-04-11T07:03:37.838Z"}
