{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01CxAp3cyzXvfpYeFo9ZYegw","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Now let me create a comprehensive summary of my findings:\n\n## Summary\n\nI've identified the root cause of the OOM error during the `logup_gkr.input_evals` phase. Here's what I found:\n\n### Pool Size Configuration\n\n**VPMM Pool Configuration** (`/home/georg/stark-backend/crates/cuda-common/src/memory_manager/vm_pool.rs`):\n- **Virtual Address Space (VA) Size**: DEFAULT_VA_SIZE = 8 TB (8 << 40 bytes) - line 29\n- **Page Size**: Defaults to device's minimum granularity (line 169), but can be overridden via `VPMM_PAGE_SIZE` environment variable\n- **Initial Pages**: Defaults to 0 (line 50), can be set via `VPMM_PAGES` environment variable\n\nThe error message shows `page_size=2097152`, which is 2 MiB - this is the granularity for physical memory allocations from cuMemCreate.\n\n### Root Cause: Large Intermediates Buffer Allocation\n\nThe issue occurs in `/home/georg/stark-backend/crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/gkr_input.rs` at **lines 147-151**:\n\n```rust\nlet buffer_size = rules.inner.buffer_size;\n// TODO[jpw]: remove magic 10\nlet is_global = buffer_size > 10;\nlet intermediates = if is_global {\n    DeviceBuffer::<EF>::with_capacity((TASK_SIZE as usize) * buffer_size as usize)\n} else {\n    DeviceBuffer::<EF>::with_capacity(1)\n};\n```\n\nWhere:\n- `TASK_SIZE = 65536` (= 2^16, defined at line 23)\n- `buffer_size` comes from interaction rules and is NOT capped (unlike zerocheck constraints which have a BUFFER_THRESHOLD of 16)\n- `EF` (extension field) = 16 bytes (4 × 32-bit Fp elements, see `/home/georg/stark-backend/crates/cuda-common/include/fpext.h`)\n\n### Memory Calculation\n\nThe allocation size is: **65536 × buffer_size × 16 bytes**\n\nExamples:\n- `buffer_size=100`: ~100 MB (50 pages of 2 MiB each)\n- `buffer_size=200`: ~200 MB (100 pages)\n- `buffer_size=500`: ~500 MB (250 pages)\n- `buffer_size=1000`: ~1 GB (500 pages)\n- `buffer_size=2048`: ~2 GB (1024 pages)\n\n### Why OOM at 6.1 GiB Used on 24 GiB GPU?\n\nThe failure at **vpmm_create_physical** (lines 540-559 in vm_pool.rs) happens because:\n\n1. **VPMM allocates pages one at a time** in the loop at line 538:\n   ```rust\n   while allocated_dst < dst + allocate_size as u64 {\n       let handle = unsafe { vpmm_create_physical(self.device_id, self.page_size) }\n   ```\n\n2. **cuMemCreate** can fail even when GPU has available memory if:\n   - The GPU memory is fragmented\n   - Other CUDA subsystems hold memory that blocks large contiguous allocations\n   - CUDA reserved memory or other driver memory limits apply\n\n3. **The pool size is uncapped** - there's no limit on how much buffer_size can grow based on the complexity of interaction constraints in the AIR specification.\n\n### Key Files Involved\n\n1. **VPMM Initialization & Configuration**:\n   - `/home/georg/stark-backend/crates/cuda-common/src/memory_manager/vm_pool.rs` (VpmmConfig, VirtualMemoryPool)\n   - Lines 29-86: Configuration with environment variable overrides\n\n2. **VPMM Physical Memory Allocation**:\n   - `/home/georg/stark-backend/crates/cuda-common/cuda/src/vpmm_shim.cu` (C++ wrapper around CUDA VMM APIs)\n   - `/home/georg/stark-backend/crates/cuda-common/src/memory_manager/cuda.rs` (Rust FFI bindings)\n\n3. **Problematic Buffer Allocation**:\n   - `/home/georg/stark-backend/crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/gkr_input.rs` (lines 147-151)\n   - `/home/georg/stark-backend/crates/cuda-backend/cuda/src/logup_zerocheck/gkr_input.cu` (corresponding CUDA kernel)\n\n4. **Allocation Failure Handling**:\n   - `/home/georg/stark-backend/crates/cuda-common/src/memory_manager/vm_pool.rs` (lines 538-576: allocation loop and error handling)\n   - `/home/georg/stark-backend/crates/cuda-common/src/error.rs` (lines 63-67: is_out_of_memory() check for error code 2)\n\n### Why It's Not Really \"Out of Memory\"\n\nThe error code `2` (cudaErrorMemoryAllocation) doesn't mean total GPU memory is exhausted. It means `cuMemCreate` couldn't allocate a single 2 MiB page, likely due to:\n- Memory fragmentation from previous allocations\n- Reserved/pinned memory from other CUDA operations\n- Virtual memory management limitations at that moment\n\nWith only 6.1 GiB of 24 GiB used, there's plenty of free memory, but it may not be available in the right form (contiguous physical pages) for cuMemCreate to succeed."}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d346b169-4c5b-4579-98c0-3e4f65b0717e","uuid":"52e390bc-841e-4524-ac1f-97a2c6bd24c1","timestamp":"2026-04-11T07:04:08.145Z","tool_use_result":{"status":"completed","prompt":"I need to understand why `vpmm_create_physical` fails with OOM during the pairing benchmark. The error is:\n```\nvpmm_create_physical failed: device=0, page_size=2097152: CudaError { code: 2, name: \"cudaErrorMemoryAllocation\", message: \"out of memory\" }\n```\n\nThis happens during `logup_gkr.input_evals` when GPU memory usage is only 6.1 GiB on a 24 GiB GPU. \n\nSearch in `/home/georg/stark-backend/crates/cuda-common` and `/home/georg/stark-backend/crates/cuda-backend` for:\n1. How the VPMM (Virtual Pool Memory Manager) is initialized - what pool size is it configured to\n2. How `vpmm_create_physical` works and when it would fail\n3. The `logup_gkr_input_evaluation` code path that triggers this allocation\n4. Any pool size limits or caps\n\nBe thorough - check both Rust and CUDA/C++ files. Report the pool size configuration and why it might OOM at 6 GiB.","agentId":"ad716248f4637f544","agentType":"Explore","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Now let me create a comprehensive summary of my findings:\n\n## Summary\n\nI've identified the root cause of the OOM error during the `logup_gkr.input_evals` phase. Here's what I found:\n\n### Pool Size Configuration\n\n**VPMM Pool Configuration** (`/home/georg/stark-backend/crates/cuda-common/src/memory_manager/vm_pool.rs`):\n- **Virtual Address Space (VA) Size**: DEFAULT_VA_SIZE = 8 TB (8 << 40 bytes) - line 29\n- **Page Size**: Defaults to device's minimum granularity (line 169), but can be overridden via `VPMM_PAGE_SIZE` environment variable\n- **Initial Pages**: Defaults to 0 (line 50), can be set via `VPMM_PAGES` environment variable\n\nThe error message shows `page_size=2097152`, which is 2 MiB - this is the granularity for physical memory allocations from cuMemCreate.\n\n### Root Cause: Large Intermediates Buffer Allocation\n\nThe issue occurs in `/home/georg/stark-backend/crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/gkr_input.rs` at **lines 147-151**:\n\n```rust\nlet buffer_size = rules.inner.buffer_size;\n// TODO[jpw]: remove magic 10\nlet is_global = buffer_size > 10;\nlet intermediates = if is_global {\n    DeviceBuffer::<EF>::with_capacity((TASK_SIZE as usize) * buffer_size as usize)\n} else {\n    DeviceBuffer::<EF>::with_capacity(1)\n};\n```\n\nWhere:\n- `TASK_SIZE = 65536` (= 2^16, defined at line 23)\n- `buffer_size` comes from interaction rules and is NOT capped (unlike zerocheck constraints which have a BUFFER_THRESHOLD of 16)\n- `EF` (extension field) = 16 bytes (4 × 32-bit Fp elements, see `/home/georg/stark-backend/crates/cuda-common/include/fpext.h`)\n\n### Memory Calculation\n\nThe allocation size is: **65536 × buffer_size × 16 bytes**\n\nExamples:\n- `buffer_size=100`: ~100 MB (50 pages of 2 MiB each)\n- `buffer_size=200`: ~200 MB (100 pages)\n- `buffer_size=500`: ~500 MB (250 pages)\n- `buffer_size=1000`: ~1 GB (500 pages)\n- `buffer_size=2048`: ~2 GB (1024 pages)\n\n### Why OOM at 6.1 GiB Used on 24 GiB GPU?\n\nThe failure at **vpmm_create_physical** (lines 540-559 in vm_pool.rs) happens because:\n\n1. **VPMM allocates pages one at a time** in the loop at line 538:\n   ```rust\n   while allocated_dst < dst + allocate_size as u64 {\n       let handle = unsafe { vpmm_create_physical(self.device_id, self.page_size) }\n   ```\n\n2. **cuMemCreate** can fail even when GPU has available memory if:\n   - The GPU memory is fragmented\n   - Other CUDA subsystems hold memory that blocks large contiguous allocations\n   - CUDA reserved memory or other driver memory limits apply\n\n3. **The pool size is uncapped** - there's no limit on how much buffer_size can grow based on the complexity of interaction constraints in the AIR specification.\n\n### Key Files Involved\n\n1. **VPMM Initialization & Configuration**:\n   - `/home/georg/stark-backend/crates/cuda-common/src/memory_manager/vm_pool.rs` (VpmmConfig, VirtualMemoryPool)\n   - Lines 29-86: Configuration with environment variable overrides\n\n2. **VPMM Physical Memory Allocation**:\n   - `/home/georg/stark-backend/crates/cuda-common/cuda/src/vpmm_shim.cu` (C++ wrapper around CUDA VMM APIs)\n   - `/home/georg/stark-backend/crates/cuda-common/src/memory_manager/cuda.rs` (Rust FFI bindings)\n\n3. **Problematic Buffer Allocation**:\n   - `/home/georg/stark-backend/crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/gkr_input.rs` (lines 147-151)\n   - `/home/georg/stark-backend/crates/cuda-backend/cuda/src/logup_zerocheck/gkr_input.cu` (corresponding CUDA kernel)\n\n4. **Allocation Failure Handling**:\n   - `/home/georg/stark-backend/crates/cuda-common/src/memory_manager/vm_pool.rs` (lines 538-576: allocation loop and error handling)\n   - `/home/georg/stark-backend/crates/cuda-common/src/error.rs` (lines 63-67: is_out_of_memory() check for error code 2)\n\n### Why It's Not Really \"Out of Memory\"\n\nThe error code `2` (cudaErrorMemoryAllocation) doesn't mean total GPU memory is exhausted. It means `cuMemCreate` couldn't allocate a single 2 MiB page, likely due to:\n- Memory fragmentation from previous allocations\n- Reserved/pinned memory from other CUDA operations\n- Virtual memory management limitations at that moment\n\nWith only 6.1 GiB of 24 GiB used, there's plenty of free memory, but it may not be available in the right form (contiguous physical pages) for cuMemCreate to succeed."}],"totalDurationMs":75067,"totalTokens":